            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I don't know if this is a twist on french toast as the submitter states or a another twist on classic peanut butter and jelly - either way it's pretty good. I just love peanut butter and if there's a different way to eat it, I'll try it. I used whole grain bread though this was delicious."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of our favorite breakfasts. I like to use whole grain or whole wheat bread and I don't use sugar in my egg wash. I will use vanilla and a little orange juice, though. My kids like this best with peanut butter and syrup instead of peanut butter and jam.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-13T07:38:20.740Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mominml"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe makes you wonder how you never thought to make this before. My son is the biggest peanut butter and jelly sandwich fan ever, and I knew that this recipe would be perfect for him. He loved it and requests it often. I made a couple with strawberry jam, and a couple with blackberry jam. Both were great. This is a great breakfast for the kids before school.",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-14T19:32:51.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JANE107"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My daughter and I loved these. I used blackberry preserves on mine &amp; my daughter chose grape jelly. Both were delightful - we'll make these again!",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-08T01:21:18.490Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LESTER68"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! This was so easy and a nice change from regular french toast. I'm on a health kick, so I liked the inclusion of peanut butter for protein, and the jam in the center allows me to eliminate all that sugar from topping it with maple syrup. I used whole wheat bread, and it turned out very moist. This is quick enough to whip up even on school mornings. I only got the recipe last week and I've served it twice already!",
            "datePublished": "2003-09-09T14:41:09.450Z"
          },
